{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund new bursaries for counselling and psychotherapy trainees in England",
        "additional_details": "Counsellors/psychotherapists help people navigate grief, trauma and emotional distress, supporting mental health, relationships and wellbeing.\r\n\r\nTraining involves supervised client work alongside academic study. Costs beyond tuition and unpaid placement commitments can create financial barriers.\r\n\r\nExisting funded routes do not support all trainees. We believe broader funding would widen access to training & help people qualify to provide safe, effective support to individuals, families & communities.\r\n",
        "background": "This scheme should also include diploma & degree routes meeting recognised professional standards. Eligible trainees on recognised diploma and degree routes should receive support with all these costs and have their tuition fees covered in full.",
